Hello, this is Sumanth. I officially started my Cloud Architect preparation on 12 May 2026.

Today marks Day 1 of my journey—learning Linux fundamentals and pushing my progress to GitHub using Git commands.
Date :12-05-2026
Day :Tuesday

1. ls
Purpose: List files and directories
Syntax:
ls
Example:
ls
Output:
Documents  Downloads  projects  notes.txt

2. ls -la
Purpose: List all files/directories including hidden files with details
Syntax:
ls -la
Example:
ls -la
Output:
drwxr-xr-x  5 sumanth sumanth 4096 May 12 10:30 .
drwxr-xr-x 10 sumanth sumanth 4096 May 12 10:00 ..
-rw-r--r--  1 sumanth sumanth 3771 May 12 10:00 .bashrc
drwxr-xr-x  2 sumanth sumanth 4096 May 12 10:20 projects

3. cp
Purpose: Copy files
Syntax:
cp source destination
Example:
cp notes.txt backup.txt
Output:
(no output if successful)

4. mv
Purpose: Move or rename files
Syntax:
mv source destination
Example:
mv backup.txt notes_backup.txt
Output:
(no output if successful)

5. rm
Purpose: Remove files
Syntax:
rm filename
Example:
rm notes.txt
Output:
(no output if successful)

6. mkdir
Purpose: Create directory
Syntax:
mkdir directory_name
Example:
mkdir projects
Output:
(no output if successful)

7. rmdir
Purpose: Remove empty directory
Syntax:
rmdir directory_name
Example:
rmdir projects
Output:
(no output if successful)

8. cat
Purpose: Read file contents
Syntax:
cat filename
Example:
cat hello.txt
Output:
Hello Linux
Welcome Sumanth

9. touch
Purpose: Create empty file
Syntax:
touch filename
Example:
touch day1.txt
Output:
(no output if successful)

10. grep
Purpose: Search specific keyword in file
Syntax:
grep "word" filename
Example:
grep "Linux" notes.txt
Output:
Linux fundamentals are important

11. grep -i
Purpose: Case-insensitive search
Syntax:
grep -i "word" filename
Example:
grep -i "linux" notes.txt
Output:
Linux fundamentals
LINUX commands
linux basics

12. find
Purpose: Search files
Syntax:
find path -name "pattern"
Example:
find . -name "*.txt"
Output:
./day1.txt
./notes.txt
./docs/report.txt

13. find .
Purpose: Search from current directory
Syntax:
find .
Example:
find .
Output:
.
./notes.txt
./projects
./projects/day1.sh

14. find . -name "*.txt"
Purpose: Find all txt files
Syntax:
find . -name "*.txt"
Example:
find . -name "*.txt"
Output:
./hello.txt
./notes/day1.txt


