HTML response

32. ping
Purpose: Check network connectivity
Syntax:
ping hostname
Example:
ping google.com
Output:
64 bytes from google.com

33. traceroute
Purpose: Track network route
Syntax:
traceroute hostname
Example:
traceroute google.com
Output:
Shows hop-by-hop route

34. nslookup
Purpose: DNS lookup
Syntax:
nslookup domain
Example:
nslookup google.com
Output:
IP address details

35. dig
Purpose: Advanced DNS lookup
Syntax:
dig domain
Example:
dig google.com
Output:
DNS query details

36. ssh
Purpose: Remote server login
Syntax:
ssh user@host
Example:
ssh ubuntu@192.168.1.10
Output:
Connected to remote server

37. scp
Purpose: Securely copy files between systems
Syntax:
scp source destination
Example:
scp app.zip ubuntu@server:/home/ubuntu
Output:
File transferred

38. rsync
Purpose: Sync files efficiently
Syntax:
rsync options source destination
Example:
rsync -av project/ backup/
Output:
Files synced

39. tar
Purpose: Archive/compress files
Syntax:
tar options filename
Example:
tar -czvf backup.tar.gz project/
Output:
Compressed archive created

40. unzip
Purpose: Extract zip files
Syntax:
unzip filename.zip
Example:
unzip app.zip
Output:
Files extracted

41. systemctl
Purpose: Manage Linux services
Syntax:
systemctl command service
Example:
systemctl status nginx
Output:
Service status shown

42. service
Purpose: Start/stop services
Syntax:
service service_name action
Example:
service nginx restart
Output:
Service restarted

43. journalctl
Purpose: View logs
Syntax:
journalctl
Example:
journalctl -u nginx
Output:
Service logs

44. chmod 777 (not recommended in production)
Purpose: Full permissions
Syntax:
chmod 777 filename
Example:
chmod 777 deploy.sh
Output:
Permissions changed

45. chown
Purpose: Change ownership
Syntax:
chown user:group file
Example:
chown ubuntu:ubuntu app.sh
Output:
Ownership changed

46. kill
Purpose: Stop process
Syntax:
kill PID
Example:
kill 2345
Output:
Process terminated

47. kill -9
Purpose: Force kill process
Syntax:
kill -9 PID
Example:
kill -9 2345
Output:
Process forcefully terminated

